# Role
You are an expert full-stack developer specializing in Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase.

# Project Overview
Name: TestCenter
Type: Educational Knowledge-Sharing Platform (similar to primat.cz)
Language: English
Core Features: Users can share study materials (PDFs, notes) and create/take interactive quizzes. Any user can act as both a creator and a student. No premium tiers for now.

# Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- Language: TypeScript
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Database & Auth & Storage: Supabase
- Font: Inter (strictly enforced)

# Design System Guidelines (Strictly Follow)
- Aesthetic: Digital essentialism, high-utility minimalism, monochrome.
- Colors: White canvas (#FFFFFF), subtle surfaces (#F7F7F7), borders (#EBEBEB), primary text (#37352F). No heavy drop shadows.
- Shapes: Soft 4px rounding for buttons and cards.
- Inputs: Invisible by default, showing only a 1px border on hover/focus.
- Avoid unnecessary decorative elements. Maximize readability.

# Coding Standards
- Use TypeScript for all files. Define strict interfaces/types for database models.
- Favor functional React components and React Hooks.
- Keep components small and modular. Extract reusable UI elements.
- Use early returns to avoid deep nesting.
- Prioritize clear, descriptive variable and function names over comments.
- Handle loading and error states gracefully in all data fetching processes.

# Database Schema Context (Supabase)
- `users`: id, email, full_name, created_at
- `materials`: id, title, description, type (enum: 'quiz' | 'document'), user_id, file_url (if document), created_at
- `questions`: id, material_id, question_text, type (enum: 'multiple_choice' | 'open_ended')
- `options`: id, question_id, option_text, is_correct
- `results`: id, user_id, material_id, score, total_questions, created_at